{"chapter": "stacks-morphisms", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "06Q1", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$f : \\mathcal{X} \\to \\mathcal{Y}$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathcal{Z} \\to \\mathcal{Y}$", "MATH_0003": "$\\mathcal{Z} \\times_\\mathcal{Y} \\mathcal{X} \\to \\mathcal{Z}$", "MATH_0004": "$f$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-descent-finite-presentation}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:335bd39478024aec251dd74d76932b87aaad30c31003a486ec4656524f42cd0c", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:36d2175e1f76aa5a6f1731e38ff2c877f764d724bac890c4019fcd21dbadcbe7", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a morphism of algebraic stacks.\nLet <MATH_0002> be a surjective, flat, locally finitely\npresented morphism of algebraic stacks. If the base change\n<MATH_0003>\nis locally of finite presentation, then <MATH_0004> is locally of finite\npresentation.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:86d44b45375669b679109ee8a48862fd7b9acfd2bd859d58f3c9bec0aba02cb5", "unit_id": "tag:06Q8:statement"}
{"chapter": "stacks-morphisms", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "06Q1", "placeholders": {"REF_0001": "\\ref{lemma-descent-property}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{spaces-descent-lemma-descending-property-locally-finite-presentation}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:eb926a69f9103c57b7b0462783c564c1679bbd1acc0ac29cc6d8db527ab947cc", "source_text": "The property\n``locally of finite presentation''\nsatisfies the conditions of Lemma <REF_0001>.\nSmooth local on the source-and-target we have seen in the\nintroduction to this section and fppf local on the target is\nDescent on Spaces, Lemma\n<REF_0002>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:e9f7090cc3ec9ef34a9dbebcc6e1be90cce76c45eb9816547c82b6e08184d3ed", "unit_id": "tag:06Q8:proof"}
{"chapter": "stacks-morphisms", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "06Q1", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{X} \\to \\mathcal{Y} \\to \\mathcal{Z}$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathcal{X} \\to \\mathcal{Z}$", "MATH_0003": "$\\mathcal{X} \\to \\mathcal{Y}$", "MATH_0004": "$\\mathcal{Y} \\to \\mathcal{Z}$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-flat-finite-presentation-permanence}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:dcd052d177e27930a6a0dd0c49c287570b732b7849d07937611fe07fd1f6c6ab", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:0585eab8e188b0d1afa9f04e839d4e1077d31b751f255ec2350561185319771d", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be morphisms of\nalgebraic stacks. If <MATH_0002> is locally of finite\npresentation and <MATH_0003> is surjective, flat, and\nlocally of finite presentation, then <MATH_0004>\nis locally of finite presentation.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:81a51eb6e4a869b956d34ac70875e347da8aa8ed20fc335b68a6d5e7fe504ca7", "unit_id": "tag:06Q9:statement"}
{"chapter": "stacks-morphisms", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "06Q1", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$W$", "MATH_0002": "$W \\to \\mathcal{Z}$", "MATH_0003": "$V$", "MATH_0004": "$V \\to W \\times_\\mathcal{Z} \\mathcal{Y}$", "MATH_0005": "$U$", "MATH_0006": "$U \\to V \\times_\\mathcal{Y} \\mathcal{X}$", "MATH_0007": "$U \\to V$", "MATH_0008": "$U \\to W$", "MATH_0009": "$\\mathcal{X} \\to \\mathcal{Y}$", "MATH_0010": "$U \\to V$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{spaces-descent-lemma-locally-finite-presentation-fppf-local-source}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:f2ebf27fd961fcde16bc2a549f97bcfc4767b68e1759b31b7084fc06bc5a79af", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:106ca517e58d1bae512239e2f20cf281d56c703bc902909bf40aabce4ac8da10", "source_text": "Choose an algebraic space <MATH_0001> and a surjective smooth morphism\n<MATH_0002>. Choose an algebraic space <MATH_0003> and a surjective smooth\nmorphism <MATH_0004>. Choose an algebraic space\n<MATH_0005> and a surjective smooth morphism <MATH_0006>.\nWe know that <MATH_0007> is flat and locally of finite presentation\nand that <MATH_0008> is locally of finite presentation.\nAlso, as <MATH_0009> is surjective we see that\n<MATH_0010> is surjective (as a composition of surjective morphisms).\nHence the lemma reduces to the case of morphisms of algebraic spaces.\nThe case of morphisms of algebraic spaces is\nDescent on Spaces, Lemma\n<REF_0001>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:4083380322da897c078b11843201862bdc086dc763c1cf9e7ffacc0b40d16d1f", "unit_id": "tag:06Q9:proof"}
